		{"id":"a25dd7e75d809036","type":"text","text":"AI for a river: what if we used a similar model to uncover shifting narratives and assign funding in the direction we want to go to amplify narratives","x":560,"y":-280,"width":250,"height":200},
		{"id":"6250f2a7ea2804d3","type":"text","text":"ALgorithms perpetuate similar narratives, if we curate via algorithm we encourage sameness","x":470,"y":430,"width":250,"height":130},
		{"id":"d0542070fb1fd774","type":"text","text":"Substack as a sign of incresing desire for narratives. What would it look like if we had the tools to define the meaning of those narratives?","x":685,"y":-10,"width":250,"height":210},
		{"id":"c150d208b0f0470b","type":"text","text":"kowledge is a form of solidified narrative that allows us to make consistent predictions about how the world works\nnarratives are an emergent propoerty of actions and interaction\nactions are at the core of the human superorganism","x":960,"y":250,"width":240,"height":330},
		{"id":"d3d9ac7c8260efb4","type":"text","text":"For knowledge production, they are suggesting narratives are the origin of knowledge, monitoring narrative directions in order to assign resources and create knowledge\n[[Unprotocolized Knowledge]]","x":760,"y":640,"width":320,"height":200},
		{"id":"b214786ee7b618b7","type":"text","text":"Connection between storyselling and branded moral ecosystems. Moral ecosystems as holonic groups: examples of building identity around narratives","x":860,"y":-300,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"6e8ffcf4b8774d39","type":"text","text":"How does this apply to how we build tech? Narratives can tell us how tech is being used and the effects it has, allowing us to create change","x":960,"y":-50,"width":250,"height":190},
		{"id":"092a9512fa1de1ce","type":"text","text":"Narratives can create real community where “storyselling” creates only ephemeral communities organized around perpetual consumption, what he elsewhere terms “swarms.”\n\n religion has become indistinguishable from interior decorating.\n\n “The fostering of local institutions, rooted in distinct, particular traditions, promises the most meaningful alternative to both the religious intolerance of the past and the secular intolerance of the present.”[](https://www.frontporchrepublic.com/2024/05/rendering-me-into-we-a-review-of-the-crisis-of-narration/#post-52206-footnote-5)\nhttps://www.frontporchrepublic.com/2024/05/rendering-me-into-we-a-review-of-the-crisis-of-narration/","x":1110,"y":-540,"width":330,"height":460},
		{"id":"da8f53187bb00b33","type":"text","text":"narratives = stories of our everyday experience\nNarratives = collective narratives","x":835,"y":-410,"width":250,"height":120},
